+@node GOMP_SPIN_YIELD
+@section @env{GOMP_SPIN_YIELD} -- Yield the CPU while busy-waiting
+@cindex Environment Variable
+@cindex Implementation specific setting
+@table @asis
+@item @emph{Description}:
+Number of spins of the busy-wait loop (@pxref{GOMP_SPINCOUNT}) after which
+a waiting thread calls @code{sched_yield}, so that other runnable threads,
+for instance a thread of the team that blocked or a thread of another
+library, can use the CPU.  The value is an integer with the same optional
+suffixes as @env{GOMP_SPINCOUNT}; @code{0} disables yielding.  If undefined,
+100 is used.  This setting is only used on Linux.
+
+@item @emph{See also}:
+@ref{GOMP_SPINCOUNT}, @ref{OMP_WAIT_POLICY}
 @end table
 
 
